  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (1S,2S)-1-Phenyl-1,2-propanediol may interact with the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype. This compound appears to target the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including Anhydrofurospongin-1, Perforamone B, and Npc168718. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of prostaglandin E2 receptor activity, suggesting a possible pathway where (1S,2S)-1-Phenyl-1,2-propanediol may modulate receptor function through the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta. The shared targeting of this subunit by multiple compounds implies a potential role in the regulation of receptor signaling, possibly through a common mechanism involving ion transport or cellular homeostasis. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
